node_modules/
dist/
apps/admin/dist/
development/coverage/
# `apps/admin` writes its own coverage output here (vitest's default `coverage/` dir, ~1.5MB of
# `coverage-final.json` alone). Same rationale as `development/coverage/` above — build output, not
# source. Added after an audit run left it untracked-but-not-ignored, where a wide `git add` would
# have swept it into a commit.
apps/admin/coverage/
# Stray ROOT coverage output. Every `test:cov*` script in package.json writes to
# `development/coverage/`, so nothing should land here -- but `apps/admin/vitest.config.ts` sets
# `reportsDirectory: "./coverage"`, which resolves against the CWD, so running that config from
# the repo root drops ~29MB at the root instead. Ignored rather than only deleted: it was
# untracked AND unignored, so a wide `git add` would have committed it.
/coverage/
# Playwright's default output dir, written when a run starts from the repo root. Untracked and,
# until now, unignored -- same wide-`git add` hazard as /coverage/ above.
/test-results/
# mkcert-issued locally-trusted dev TLS cert + private key, shared by BOTH dev servers
# (`server.https` in `apps/admin/vite.config.ts`, and the API's own gate in
# `apps/website/src/server/runtime/boot/dev-tls.ts`). Machine-specific, never shared or
# committed — each contributor runs `mkcert -install` once and regenerates their own. Moved here
# from `apps/admin/.certs*/` so one directory serves both servers; the toggle is still a single
# rename: `mv .certs .certs.disabled` / `mv .certs.disabled .certs`, now from the repo root.
/.certs*/
*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
# The template is the one .env file that MUST be tracked — it is how a fresh clone learns which
# variables a local boot needs. `development/scripts/dev.mjs` loads `.env` (never this file).
!.env.example
# sites/ holds every SITE's own runtime data -- one folder per site (`sites/<name>/`), each owning
# its content.db + WAL sidecars, uploads/, themes/, skills/, agent-plugins/, the ADR-041 ops
# journals, restore points, and out/ build output. None of it is source, and none of it may ever be
# replaced by an upgrade: that is the whole point of the 2026-08-27 move off `infra/`, which had
# runtime data and the product's own theme tree (then `src/themes/`, now `content/themes/`)
# tangled together.
# README.md stays tracked so the directory exists in a fresh clone -- openContentDb does not create
# its parent, so an absent sites/ fails boot with SQLITE_CANTOPEN.
#
# 2026-08-31: sites/ is now TRACKED. Ignoring it wholesale meant every git-based deploy (Fly,
# Railway, Render, App Runner) booted a container with no content.db, no themes and no theme.json --
# a correct image with no site in it. Tracking the site is what makes a deploy carry its content.
# Still never tracked, and these must stay ignored:
#   - content.db itself: this is each site's LIVE, growing database (real chat transcripts, session
#     auth log, sealed provider credentials, ...) -- committing it verbatim would bloat git history
#     without bound and leak real secrets/PII. `npm run seed:site` (development/scripts/seed-site.mjs)
#     produces the thing that SHOULD be committed instead: a pruned, VACUUMed copy at the sibling path
#     `content.seed.db`, deliberately NOT matched by this pattern so it stays tracked. See that
#     script's header for the full prune rationale and for what still has to promote `content.seed.db`
#     into the path a deployed container actually boots from.
#   - WAL/shm sidecars: transient, and a sidecar committed against a mismatched content.db
#     corrupts reads on checkout.
#   - restore points + .bak snapshots: ~67M of point-in-time DB copies, each a full binary blob.
#   - out/: build output, regenerated.
sites/*/content.db
sites/*/content.db-wal
sites/*/content.db-shm
sites/*/content.db.bak-*
sites/*/restore-point-*.db
sites/*/out/
# 2026-09-06: commit 0fb84ae0 split chat history out of content.db into its own per-site
# chat.db, but added no ignore rule for the new file -- the rule above protects content.db's
# "real chat transcripts" (see comment at the top of this block), and those transcripts moved out
# from under it. Closing that gap here, plus the undated .bak forms the dated
# `content.db.bak-*` rule above doesn't reach (content.db.bak, content.db.predelete.bak, and
# chat.db's own .bak) and the restore-point WAL/shm sidecars (the bare rule above only matches the
# .db file itself, the same sidecar gap content.db already gets explicit rules for).
sites/*/chat.db
sites/*/chat.db-wal
sites/*/chat.db-shm
# Covers content.db.bak, content.db.predelete.bak, and chat.db.bak in one durable rule instead of
# naming each snapshot variant -- any future undated .bak dropped directly in a site dir is a
# point-in-time DB copy, same class as the dated content.db.bak-* rule above.
sites/*/*.bak
sites/*/restore-point-*.db-wal
sites/*/restore-point-*.db-shm
# `content.seed.db` itself IS tracked (see above), but its own WAL/shm sidecars are the same
# open-connection artifact as content.db's own -- e.g. merely opening it read-only with
# better-sqlite3 creates them -- and committing one against a mismatched content.seed.db would
# corrupt reads on checkout the same way. Never meaningful content; delete on sight.
sites/*/content.seed.db-wal
sites/*/content.seed.db-shm
# ADR-041 ops journals (same live-runtime-data class as content.db above, not source): the OLD
# root-level `ops/database-journal.db` rule below predates the 2026-08-27 move of per-site runtime
# data under `sites/<name>/`, so it never reached `sites/<name>/ops/...` and these were never
# actually excluded once sites/ started being tracked. Sidecars included for the same
# open-WAL-corrupts-on-checkout reason as content.db's own.
sites/*/ops/*.db
sites/*/ops/*.db-wal
sites/*/ops/*.db-shm

# 2026-09-09: `EnvOrFileKeyring`'s generated-file fallback for TOVU_INTEGRATIONS_ROOT_KEY
# (`apps/website/src/features/webhooks/keyring.env.ts`) now defaults to `sites/.tovu/
# integrations-root-key.hex` in production (a SIBLING of every sites/<name>/ folder, never inside
# one — see sites/README.md's own section on why). `sites/` itself is TRACKED as of 2026-08-31
# (comment above) so a git-based deploy carries seed CONTENT — this is the opposite: real secret
# material that must never reach git, whether from a git-based deploy's own working tree or a
# local run with TOVU_RUNTIME_MODE=production set for testing. Ignored wholesale, not just the
# key file itself, in case this directory ever grows a second file.
sites/.tovu/

# `tovu theme migrate`'s scratch output (migrate-theme.ts's createStagingDir) — deliberately left on
# disk as a sibling of the real theme folder for dry-run/failure inspection, never meant to be
# committed. ARCH-001 (2026-08-19): two of these were swept into a commit by a broad `git add` and
# discovered as extra copies of the theme they were migrating (see MIGRATION_STAGING_DIR_PREFIX in
# src/features/theme/theme.ts, which also excludes this pattern from theme discovery as a second,
# independent layer — this entry only stops it from being committed again).
content/themes/**/.tovu-migrate-staging-*

# Vendored dev toolkit — cloned separately, has its own git history (not part of Tovu)
AI-Dev-Shop/

.playwright-mcp/

# Playwright VRT (AW-2) — local run artifacts only; baseline screenshots under
# development/e2e/**/*-snapshots/ ARE committed (checked baselines, not artifacts).
test-results/
# Playwright's per-config output dirs (`development/playwright.*.config.ts` each set their own
# `outputDir`), ~27MB of traces/screenshots across the two that exist today. Same class as
# `test-results/` above, which only matched the bare name.
development/test-results-*/
development/playwright-report/
blob-report/
# Regenerated-on-every-run screenshots (e.g. connectors-screenshot.spec.ts), not checked baselines
# — those live under `*-snapshots/` above and stay committed. Same "artifact, not fixture" split.
development/e2e/__screenshots__/
# Ad-hoc debug captures and one-off probe scripts written during interactive runs (~4.7MB today).
# Same "artifact, not fixture" split as the two entries above: nothing here is a checked baseline.
development/e2e/.artifacts/

# stray/local artifacts (do not track)
admin-page.png
# Ad-hoc verification screenshots agents drop at the repo root (Playwright runs, manual checks).
# Root-anchored so it only covers this directory -- every tracked .png in the repo lives under a
# subdirectory (content/brand/icons/, ADS-memory/reports/), none at the root itself.
/*.png
# Root-level scratch dir agents already use for local-only artifacts (dropped stash patches,
# screenshots) -- distinct from ADS-memory/.local-artifacts/ ignored above. Found untracked-but-
# unignored during the 2026-09-05 cleanup, same wide-`git add` hazard as /coverage/ above.
/.local-artifacts/
# Playwright accessibility-tree dump from an interactive exploration pass; regenerate on demand.
explore-snapshot.md
# Stray SQLite journal written outside infra/ by a local run. Runtime data, not source.
ops/database-journal.db
:memory:.snapshot-newsletter-*
:memory:.snapshot-comments-*
:memory:.snapshot-store-*
.claude/settings.local.json
# ADS-memory: only the pipeline artifacts are committed. Everything else in the
# workspace (docs/, governance/, knowledge/, sessions/, meta/, .local-artifacts/,
# tmp/) is local-only. Excluding the direct children rather than `ADS-memory/**`
# is what lets git still descend into the three re-included directories.
ADS-memory/*
!ADS-memory/reports/
!ADS-memory/specs/
!ADS-memory/specs_as_built/
# Multi-megabyte generated dump; regenerate from the Shopify Admin API instead.
development/other-repos-specs/shopify_specs/schema-dumps/
.mcp.json
# Per-run MCP config the agent daemon writes for each spawned CLI (`mcp-injection.ts`), named
# `.mcp.jini-<runId>.json`. Transient and machine-specific; one is left behind per run.
.mcp.jini-*.json

# `npm run link:jini`'s record of which @jini-ai/* packages it npm-linked and where, so
# `npm run unlink:jini` can clean up. Machine-specific (points at a local Jini checkout path) —
# never meant to be shared or committed.
development/.jini-link-state.json

# Pre-npm-switch copies of the three package.json files, back when @jini-ai/* deps were
# `file:../Jini/packages/*`. Kept as a manual escape hatch: `npm run link:jini` is the supported way
# back to a local Jini checkout, but these let you restore the old manifests verbatim if that fails.
# Machine-specific, never committed.
development/.jini-local-backup/

# Private business/fundraising material — investor lists, contact details, deal docs.
# Already covered for `ADS-memory/docs/business/` by the `ADS-memory/*` rule above; this entry
# guards the repo-root path too, since `docs/business/` is where it originally lived and a
# recreated folder there would otherwise be tracked. NOTE: ignoring only stops FUTURE commits —
# the investor list is still reachable in git history (commits 7363fd4a, 1b3bee71, baa4ea1e) and
# requires a history rewrite before this repo can be published.
docs/business/
